# .gitignore
# Git will completely ignore everything listed in this file.
# Nothing here is ever uploaded to GitHub.

# === SECRETS — the most important lines in this file ===
# .env will hold your OpenAI API key. A leaked key can cost you real money.
.env

# === The virtual environment ===
# Over 100 MB of downloaded libraries. Anyone can rebuild it from
# requirements.txt with one command, so there is no reason to upload it.
.venv/
venv/

# === Python's temporary compiled files ===
# Python creates these automatically to run faster. They are not source code.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# === Testing leftovers ===
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# === Databases our program creates while running ===
# These are generated by the program, not written by us. They are rebuilt
# every time the app runs, so uploading them adds nothing.
data/*.db
data/*.sqlite3
data/chroma/

# === Editor and operating-system clutter ===
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini